# Secrets — never tracked
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Data and model artefacts
# **The parquet snapshots are tracked, reversing the original decision** (20 Aug 2026).
# They stayed out of git as a matter of habit, and the habit cost more than the 800 KB it
# saved: every cache-gated test — the train/live parity sweep, the offline smoke path, the
# whole study grid — was SKIPPED in CI, so a mechanism the project relies on ran nowhere
# except on one laptop. CLAUDE.md §3: a mechanism that can be skipped by a flag is a
# mechanism only when the flag is off.
#
# It also makes `data_snapshot_last_bar` mean something. §7 requires every result to name
# the snapshot it ran against; a snapshot nobody else has is a name, not a reference.
#
# The quality report stays tracked for the reason it always was: it records what the data
# looked like when a result was produced, which a reader of that result cannot
# reconstruct. Note the pattern: `data_cache/` would exclude the directory itself and make
# the negations below unreachable.
data_cache/*
!data_cache/quality_report.json
!data_cache/*.parquet
checkpoints/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
